# Relayer mnemonics. Never commit these: they control funded accounts on live
# chains. Generated by keys.sh, mode 600, in a 700 directory.
.hermes_mnemonics/
# Channel ids written by bringup.sh — derived state, regenerate rather than commit.
# Globbed because the natural move before a chain reset is to keep a copy
# (.ibc_channels.stale, .bak), and those are derived state too.
.ibc_channels*
# Unsigned transactions emitted by setup_peers.sh for a signer whose key is
# not on this machine. Derived state: regenerate rather than commit.
.unsigned/
